In article <1993Aug3.222827.13027@twg.com>, blume@twg.com (David Blume) writes:
> I have two recommendations for the next patch of NetHack.
> 
> 1.  Make the floating eye freeze time-out shorter.  Or, occasionally have
>     combat wake you up.  (I've seen this elsewhere.  Where was that?)
>     There's something a little too maddening about watching a newt nibble
>     you to death...
 
Hmmm.  What I'd like to see is a shorter timeout, but more active eyes.
Say, a paralysis range of several squares, but a timeout of only 1-5
turns (maybe increase that inversely proportional to your distance from
the eye).  Sort of a paralysis ray attack.

> 2.  Have the instant death by poisoned attack (natural 20) modified.  I'd
>     like to see it turn into a serious trouble, like eating a tainted corpse.
>     You should have a round or two to apply your unicorn horn, quaff extra
>     healing, or pray to your god.

I like this one, but I'm probably only saying that since I just lost a 
13th level knight with AC -10, and various goodies to a giant spider.  :-(
It's got to be said though, instant deaths are the one thing I really don't
like about the game.  And before anyone says "well, you can always get
poison resistance",  I did try.  Numerous killer bee corpses and application
of a unicorn horn did no good at all.  Bad luck, I know, but it was still
a tad irritating :-)

